<title>USA: Flextronics stake raised by investor.</title>
<headline>Flextronics stake raised by investor.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York investor Ronald Baron said Tuesday he raised his stake in Flextronics International Ltd to 1,931,600 ordinary shares, or 14.5 percent, from 13.2 percent held previously.</p>
<p>In a filing with Securities and Exchange Commission, Baron said his latest transactions include buying 100,000 ordinary shares between Dec 2 and Jan 24 at $26.50 to $35.0625 per share.</p>
<p>Flextronics, which makes circuit boards, is based in Singapore.</p>
